other contributors, used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC-BY 4.0):

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Source: Twemoji (maintained fork: https://github.com/jdecked/twemoji),
obtained via the emoji-datasource-twitter npm package
(https://www.npmjs.com/package/emoji-datasource-twitter), which packages
these graphics for build tooling under its own MIT-licensed wrapper code —
the graphics themselves remain CC-BY 4.0 per that package's own README.

Copyright 2020 Twitter, Inc and other contributors.

Files are named by their emoji's own Unicode codepoint sequence in
lowercase hex, hyphen-joined (e.g. 1f1fa-1f1f8.png for the US flag) — see
MediaPickerDialog.js's flag-rendering code for how the filename is derived
from a glyph at render time.
